{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 6,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.099,
            0.105,
            0.127,
            0.118
          ],
          "content": "44"
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.782,
            0.104,
            0.899,
            0.121
          ],
          "content": "MATHEMATICS"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.138,
            0.828,
            0.158
          ],
          "content": "**Example 6 :** Find the dimensions of the prayer hall discussed in Section 4.1."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.164,
            0.901,
            0.223
          ],
          "content": "**Solution :** In Section 4.1, we found that if the breadth of the hall is x m, then x satisfies the equation $2x^{2}+x-300=0$ . Applying the factorisation method, we write this equation as"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.227,
            0.518,
            0.246
          ],
          "content": "2x^{2}-24x+25x-300=0",
          "image_source": "images/page_6_equation_4.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.231,
            0.252,
            0.518,
            0.272
          ],
          "content": "2x\\left (x-12  \\right ) +25\\left (x-12  \\right ) =0",
          "image_source": "images/page_6_equation_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.279,
            0.139,
            0.296
          ],
          "content": "i.e.,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.305,
            0.278,
            0.518,
            0.297
          ],
          "content": "(x - 12)(2x + 25) = 0",
          "image_source": "images/page_6_equation_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.304,
            0.9,
            0.342
          ],
          "content": "So, the roots of the given equation are $x = 12   or   x = -12.5$ . Since x is the breadth of the hall, it cannot be negative."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.347,
            0.71,
            0.367
          ],
          "content": "Thus, the breadth of the hall is 12 m. Its length = 2x + 1 = 25 m."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.412,
            0.387,
            0.586,
            0.406
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "EXERCISE 4.2"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.417,
            0.749,
            0.435
          ],
          "content": "**1.** Find the roots of the following quadratic equations by factorisation:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.171,
            0.447,
            0.342,
            0.465
          ],
          "content": "(i) $x^{2}-3x-10=0$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.542,
            0.447,
            0.702,
            0.466
          ],
          "content": "(ii) $2x^{2} + x - 6 = 0$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.476,
            0.401,
            0.498
          ],
          "content": "(iii) $\\sqrt{2} x^{2} + 7x + 5\\sqrt{2} = 0$"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.537,
            0.469,
            0.711,
            0.506
          ],
          "content": "2x^{2}-x+\\frac{1}{8}=0",
          "image_source": "images/page_6_equation_15.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.506,
            0.372,
            0.523
          ],
          "content": "(v) $100x^{2}-20x+1=0$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.529,
            0.497,
            0.548
          ],
          "content": "**2.** Solve the problems given in Example 1."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.552,
            0.633,
            0.569
          ],
          "content": "**3.** Find two numbers whose sum is 27 and product is 182."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.573,
            0.759,
            0.592
          ],
          "content": "**4.** Find two consecutive positive integers, sum of whose squares is 365."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.595,
            0.901,
            0.631
          ],
          "content": "**5.** The altitude of a right triangle is 7 cm less than its base. If the hypotenuse is 13 cm, find the other two sides."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.635,
            0.902,
            0.706
          ],
          "content": "**6.** A cottage industry produces a certain number of pottery articles in a day. It was observed on a particular day that the cost of production of each article (in rupees) was 3 more than twice the number of articles produced on that day. If the total cost of production on that day was \\` 90, find the number of articles produced and the cost of each article."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.719,
            0.325,
            0.737
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "4.4 Nature of Roots"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.745,
            0.516,
            0.765
          ],
          "content": "The equation $ax^{2} + bx + c = 0$ are given by"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.349,
            0.773,
            0.545,
            0.821
          ],
          "content": "x = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}",
          "image_source": "images/page_6_equation_24.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.823,
            0.902,
            0.916
          ],
          "content": "If $b ^ { 2 }   -   4 a c   >   0$ , we get two distinct real roots $- { \\frac { b } { 2 a } } + { \\frac { \\sqrt { b ^ { 2 } - 4 a c } } { 2 a } }$ and $-   { \\frac { b } { 2 a } } - { \\frac { \\sqrt { b ^ { 2 } - 4 a c } } { 2 a } } .$"
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.435,
            0.967,
            0.563,
            0.982
          ],
          "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
        }
